NAME

ulibUpdateFile - Updates a file catalogue entry to disk


SYNOPSIS

UBYTE ulibUpdateFile(struct FileCat *File1)
                              a0


DESCRIPTION

This function updates the file catalogue entry <File1> (stored in memory) to
disk.

<File1> must already be present in the catalogue, and its date uploaded,
section number, and name must NOT have been changed; in order to change these
elements, the ulibRelinkFile() function must be used.

This function simply overwrites the disk based version of the file catalogue
entry with the provided version.  No key linking or unlinking is performed,
thus the need for the above restrictions.


RETURN VALUES

0 - Failure (usually because the file is not present in the catalogue)
1 - Success
